"notes": "Cash basis county, no business-type funds. Governmental funds statement (p4) Total Governmental Funds column used; beginning/ending cash = beginning/ending fund balances (8,236,814 / 7,959,096). Taxes 4,344,140 split into property/motor vehicle/lodging using the Statement of Activities general receipts (p2), which sum exactly; inheritance tax is its own line. Balance sheet: Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1), no liabilities. Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p8) is by department; its function subtotals differ slightly from the statement's General Fund column (p5 gen gov 2,648,210 / safety 1,257,550 / works 56,755 vs schedule 2,651,801 / 1,260,766 / 57,558) because the statement reclassifies capital outlay 7,610, but totals tie at 4,022,665. General Fund budget schedule excludes the Inheritance Tax Fund (GASB 54 note p11), so that fund's column from p5 is recorded separately; p5 General Fund column itself not repeated (no double counting). Non-major combining schedule (p6-7, 11+ funds) recorded using its Total column p7; its transfers in 28,546 / out 48,945 net to the statement's (20,399) on p4. Debt Service budget schedule has a single disbursements line; split into principal/interest from p4. Transfers in/out of 863,269 each = General 20,399 + Road 842,870 in and General 842,870 + nonmajor 20,399 out. Page 11 is the budgetary note. Read pages 1-11 of 11. Local 863,660 split by the Statement of Activities receipts (p2); the 2,658 residual (p2 receipts net 7,411 lower than p4) stays in other."
